{"id":"n3a27a31136","headline":"Peace talks are in doubt as the U.S. seizes an Iranian ship","summary":"President Trump said a US delegation will travel to Pakistan to resume talks, but Tehran expressed reluctance after the US seized an Iranian cargo ship in the Strait of Hormuz. The talks aim to end the war with Iran.","why":"The Strait of Hormuz carries a large share of global seaborne oil, so disruptions there move crude prices and shipping costs.","category":"geopolitics","event_type":"geopolitics","importance":3,"flag":null,"market_moving":true,"location":{"place":"Strait of Hormuz","country":"Iran","lat":26.6,"lon":56.3,"region":"me"},"entities":[],"links":[],"source":{"name":"Public Radio Tulsa","url":"https://www.publicradiotulsa.org/npr-national-news/2026-04-20/peace-talks-in-doubt-as-u-s-seizes-iranian-ship"},"sources":[{"name":"Public Radio Tulsa","url":"https://www.publicradiotulsa.org/npr-national-news/2026-04-20/peace-talks-in-doubt-as-u-s-seizes-iranian-ship"}],"published_at":"2026-04-20T07:02:32Z","retrieved_at":"2026-11-17T16:57:23Z","official":false,"ai_summary":true,"content_hash":"ef1646b91bfe60d8","impacts":[],"why_moved":"Stalled talks and the seizure of an Iranian vessel in the Strait of Hormuz raise the risk of further disruption to shipping through a key oil route.","backfilled":true,"backfilled_at":"2026-11-17T16:57:23Z","backfill_provenance":{"version":"gdelt-backfill-v1","original_published_at":"2026-04-20T07:02:32Z","feed_url":"https://data.gdeltproject.org/gdeltv2/","discovered_via":"GDELT GKG 2.1","gdelt_seen":"2026-04-20T12:00:00Z","publisher_country_gdelt":"PK","description_from":"publisher page metadata"},"image":{"kind":"topic","file":"photos/oil-tanker-ship-5404576.jpg","alt":"oil tanker ship (illustration)","credit":"PDC23","license":"Pixabay Content License","license_url":"https://pixabay.com/service/license-summary/","source":"Pixabay","source_url":"https://pixabay.com/photos/port-ship-rozenburg-bone-leak-5404576/"}}